id: metallic
name: Metallic
kind: battlefield
envQuality: true
hardnessMin: 3
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Metal underfoot. Hardness Rank 3 at the least.
text: >
  Metallic: This Square is made of metal. It must have a Hardness Rank of 3+. If this
  Environmental Quality is applied through an effect, remove all other Environmental
  Qualities on this Feature.

---

# "It must have a Hardness Rank of 3+."
#
# A floor rather than a shift, which is the difference between this and Glass: glass over
# stone is one Rank harder than the stone, and metal is metal whatever was there before.
#
# `hardnessMin: 3` on a Quality reads the same way it does on an Environment - the lowest
# Rank this allows - so the picker on the tab offers Rank 3 upwards while it is ticked, and
# a Rank already picked below that is pulled up to it.
#
# --- What is not built ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "If this Environmental Quality is applied through an effect, remove all other
# Environmental Qualities on this Feature." Nothing in this system applies one through an
# effect, so the clause has nothing to fire on - the same as Glass's.
